{"id":12,"result":{"id":"2026-10-30-22-11-08-room","dir":"/tmp/rec-Acvh6p/.quorum/rooms/2026-10-30-22-11-08-room","topic":"Should we add a cache to the product API?","state":"paused","agents":[{"id":"architect","cli":"mock","persona":"architect"},{"id":"skeptic","cli":"mock","persona":"skeptic"},{"id":"pragmatist","cli":"mock","persona":"pragmatist"}],"left":[],"support":{"assistant":{"cli":"mock"},"chair":{"cli":"mock"},"scribe":{"cli":"mock"},"floor":{"cli":"mock"}},"digest":"- Agreed: an in-process LRU per instance, no Redis yet.\n- Contested: staleness during bulk import (skeptic).\n- Plan is at v2.","tuning":{"parallel":2,"turnCap":40,"quotaWarn":0.75,"quotaStop":0.9},"focus":"should-we-add-a-cache","topics":[{"slug":"should-we-add-a-cache","title":"Should we add a cache to the product API?","closed":false},{"slug":"cache-consistency-during-bulk-import","title":"Cache consistency during bulk import","closed":false}],"docs":[{"slug":"plan","version":2,"kind":"plan","accepted":2}],"pending":[{"type":"suggestion","id":4,"from":"assistant","action":"steer","args":["Settle the staleness limit first, then the bulk-import strategy."],"why":"","seq":39,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:15.185Z"}],"events":[{"type":"resumed","seq":1,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:08.316Z"},{"type":"topic.raised","slug":"should-we-add-a-cache","title":"Should we add a cache to the product API?","by":"human","seq":2,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:08.317Z"},{"type":"topic.focus","slug":"should-we-add-a-cache","by":"human","seq":3,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:08.317Z"},{"type":"message","from":"human","to":"room","text":"Should we add a cache to the product API?","seq":4,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:08.317Z"},{"type":"aside","from":"assistant","text":"For a caching decision I'd start with three people who will disagree usefully: someone to propose the design, someone to attack its consistency story, and someone to keep it simple.","kind":"note","seq":5,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.957Z"},{"type":"suggestion","id":1,"from":"assistant","action":"add","args":["architect","mock"],"why":"proposes the design and writes the plan","seq":6,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.957Z"},{"type":"suggestion","id":2,"from":"assistant","action":"add","args":["skeptic","mock"],"why":"will press on consistency and failure modes","seq":7,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.957Z"},{"type":"suggestion","id":3,"from":"assistant","action":"add","args":["pragmatist","mock"],"why":"keeps scope and operational cost honest","seq":8,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.957Z"},{"type":"agent.joined","agent":"architect","persona":"architect","cli":"mock","seq":9,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.958Z"},{"type":"suggestion.resolved","id":1,"accepted":true,"seq":10,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.960Z"},{"type":"agent.joined","agent":"skeptic","persona":"skeptic","cli":"mock","seq":11,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.960Z"},{"type":"suggestion.resolved","id":2,"accepted":true,"seq":12,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.961Z"},{"type":"agent.joined","agent":"pragmatist","persona":"pragmatist","cli":"mock","seq":13,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.961Z"},{"type":"suggestion.resolved","id":3,"accepted":true,"seq":14,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:09.961Z"},{"type":"message","from":"skeptic","to":"room","text":"Before we pick a cache: what's the consistency requirement? If a price changes, how long may a stale price be shown? Nobody has said.","seq":15,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:10.765Z"},{"type":"message","from":"architect","to":"room","text":"Starting point: an in-process LRU per instance. About 90% of our reads are product lookups by id, so a read-through cache in front of the repository gets most of the win without new infrastructure.","seq":16,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:11.014Z"},{"type":"floor","picks":[{"agent":"skeptic","why":"has something to add on this","replyTo":16}],"seq":17,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:11.165Z"},{"type":"topic.raised","slug":"cache-consistency-during-bulk-import","title":"Cache consistency during bulk import","by":"skeptic","why":"it needs its own answer before we ship","seq":18,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:11.378Z"},{"type":"message","from":"pragmatist","to":"room","text":"Agree with an in-process LRU for now. Redis is one more thing to run, and we don't have the traffic to justify it yet.","seq":19,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:11.577Z"},{"type":"floor","picks":[{"agent":"architect","why":"has something to add on this","replyTo":19}],"seq":20,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:11.728Z"},{"type":"doc.revised","slug":"plan","version":1,"kind":"plan","by":"architect","note":"first draft","seq":21,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:11.930Z"},{"type":"message","from":"skeptic","to":"room","text":"For single writes, yes. But bulk import writes thousands of rows; if we only invalidate at the end, readers see a half-updated catalog for the whole import.","replyTo":16,"seq":22,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:12.060Z"},{"type":"floor","picks":[{"agent":"pragmatist","why":"has something to add on this","replyTo":22}],"seq":23,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:12.213Z"},{"type":"message","from":"architect","to":"room","text":"I've put up a first plan (plan v1): LRU, 30 s TTL, invalidate on the three write paths. @skeptic, does a 30 second bound answer your staleness question?","replyTo":19,"seq":24,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:12.632Z"},{"type":"message","from":"pragmatist","to":"room","text":"30 seconds of staleness is fine for product pages; checkout re-reads prices anyway.","replyTo":22,"seq":25,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:12.744Z"},{"type":"floor","picks":[{"agent":"skeptic","why":"has something to add on this","replyTo":24}],"seq":26,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:12.783Z"},{"type":"floor","picks":[{"agent":"architect","why":"has something to add on this","replyTo":25}],"seq":27,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:12.934Z"},{"type":"doc.revised","slug":"plan","version":2,"kind":"plan","by":"architect","note":"per-batch invalidation, load test","seq":28,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:13.136Z"},{"type":"message","from":"skeptic","to":"room","text":"If we invalidate per batch instead of at the end, I can live with it, as long as the TTL stays short.","replyTo":24,"seq":29,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:13.538Z"},{"type":"message","from":"architect","to":"room","text":"@skeptic is right about bulk imports. Plan v2 invalidates per batch instead of at the end, and adds a load test before we turn it on.","replyTo":25,"seq":30,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:13.790Z"},{"type":"doc.accepted","slug":"plan","version":2,"by":"chair","seq":31,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:14.103Z"},{"type":"paused","reason":"milestone: plan v2 accepted","seq":32,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:14.103Z"},{"type":"message","from":"chair","to":"room","text":"Plan v2 answers every objection raised so far.","seq":33,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:14.103Z"},{"type":"aside","from":"human","text":"where are we?","seq":34,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:14.104Z"},{"type":"aside","from":"assistant","text":"- Agreed: an in-process LRU per instance, no Redis yet.\n- Contested: staleness during bulk import (skeptic).\n- Plan is at v2.","kind":"digest","seq":35,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:14.828Z"},{"type":"aside","from":"assistant","text":"They converged on the LRU quickly; the only real disagreement is bulk-import staleness. Nothing needs you yet.","kind":"note","seq":36,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:14.828Z"},{"type":"docs.updated","files":["decisions.md","open-questions.md","code-notes.md"],"by":"scribe","seq":37,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:14.902Z"},{"type":"aside","from":"assistant","text":"In short: they agree on a simple in-process cache and are now arguing about how stale data may get. The skeptic's bulk-import concern is the open thread; the plan is at v2.","kind":"answer","seq":38,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:15.184Z"},{"type":"suggestion","id":4,"from":"assistant","action":"steer","args":["Settle the staleness limit first, then the bulk-import strategy."],"why":"","seq":39,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:15.185Z"},{"type":"message","from":"human","to":"room","text":"Keep the TTL under a minute.","seq":40,"ts":"2026-10-30T22:11:15.186Z"}]}}
